# Every file in a generated Terp app is stored and checked out with LF.
#
# The app's canonical toolchain is Linux: the gate, the agent and the whole
# workbench run inside containers that write LF. A Windows checkout that
# converts to CRLF therefore rewrites every line the moment a container touches
# a file — a 7-line change lands as a 900-line diff, which defeats review and
# `git blame`. Pinning eol=lf keeps the working copy byte-identical on every
# platform, so a diff only ever shows what actually changed.
#
# `text=auto` still lets Git detect binaries and leave them alone.
* text=auto eol=lf
